Low transaction volumes for any of our brokerage asset classes generally result in reduced revenues. Under these
conditions, our profitability is adversely affected since many of our costs are fixed. In addition, although less common, some of our
financial services or commercial real estate transaction revenues are determined on the basis of the value of transactions or on spreads.
For these reasons, substantial decreases in trading volume, declining prices, and/or reduced spreads could have material adverse
effects on our businesses, financial condition, results of operations and prospects.
